{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for R1 revision 9, exact head ba556e963b45793001e590fb5a7d0c4ba40669d8, all four filed subjects.\n\nP2 — Restrict discarding prefetched inputs to turns that write no entry. Main line 4681 says inputs are discarded and nothing charged whenever an input is refused. Sections 5.2/5.3 (1702–1713) require written refusals of genesis, request and advisory inputs to retain the facts they read. The concrete lane's unpin handler (lane-instantiations.md:278) reads a manifest, then can refuse not-the-owner; that refusal must retain its source and manifest. Line 4681 currently directs the opposite. State that inputs are discarded when no entry is written; a written refusal retains and charges its read inputs in its transaction, drawing on the appropriate duty reservation. This is a contradictory design instruction, not a claim of an executed runtime failure.\n\nP2 — Derive the temporary reserve from the finite timed closure, or narrow its domain. Main lines 4783–4786 offer sum(max of timed item types) + 1 as the entry reserve for definitions with no sends, settles or opening operations. The timed grammar at 1395–1421 admits one non-hold item (max 1) with two acyclic rules A -\u003e B -\u003e final at the same fixed past deadline. Both transitions leave their old states. It needs two timed entries plus a closing checkpoint, three entries; the stated formula gives two. After ordinary work fills budget minus two, both timed entries fit but the closing checkpoint does not. Sections 17.2 and the six conditions at 4746–4777 already require recursive duties and the full guarantee, so those conditions reject the inadequate reserve; the defect is the asserted derived formula/domain, not an authorization in the complete contract or a newly demonstrated source failure. Compute the worst-case finite timed closure and matching bytes, plus checkpoint, or expressly limit this shortcut to one terminal transition per item.\n\nThe previous four finding groups are repaired in this candidate design: pending acknowledgments count historical outstanding requests rather than transport buffers; byte reservations include newly retained inputs and staged snapshots; closedBy is a local typed self reference; and job decidedBy is a typed value established by check, error or timeout. Advisory send/attention grammar and final/copy wording are consistent. These repairs are proposal-level conclusions, not implementation closure.\n\nCoverage: full collective current reading of main 1–5195, corrections 1–384 and lane instantiations 1–419; root independently read complete section 17, its refusal and timed grammar dependencies, prior findings, and current dispositions. Main 1–3200 and all its changed hunks were independently read by the installation audit; the starter audit read main 3201–5195, corrections and the lane companion in full. Admission inventory's complete prior reading transfers by identical Git blob b27b17b6d86559fd18be688c2134b48ad75efe9a at adopted 05244cf, prior a549aac and this exact head. Root did not independently read every byte of the combined diff. All four artifacts were inspected and ordinary prepare confirmed evidence-only binding to request 1e85696dfd5140fff8d0f918c87f19f01b84ca45.\n\nArchitecture: recursive duty accounting and replay custody are coherent in direction, but the two instructions above must agree before adoption. Security: evidence bounds, destination/configuration trust and freshness, and the foreign-definition name beside an uncovered digest remain explicit joint-owner duties (R1-28, R1-30, R1-33); this review neither closes them nor duplicates their commissions. Simplification: use the existing no-entry distinction and one explicit finite-closure rule instead of adding a parallel refusal or timer model. All original common follow-through and actual I1 deltas 79–95 remain in scope, with source repair qualifications preserved. Adopted R0/R2/R3/R4 and complete product scope remain the bases; candidate R1 revision 9 remains unadopted. Static reading only: no tests, builds, installs, private diagnostics, source edits or external effects were executed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9e0a42de35e4bdbc4aac22b4c3fb7d6e1f4e5696","binding":"evidence-only","head":"ba556e963b45793001e590fb5a7d0c4ba40669d8","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e027f00c1b648f124012bde9c987d71ff6ab2340\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a85ba6c186b879276b697a41b0834edc0957c4af","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}